{"title":"1967 AHSME Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The difference in the areas of two similar triangles is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> square feet, and the ratio of the larger area to the smaller is the square of an integer.  The area of the smaller triange, in square feet, is an integer, and one of its sides is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> feet.  The corresponding side of the larger triangle, in feet, is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/e/6be33c9a0809b8cd2caaad9109e70872ea2ea8fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 12\\quad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 9\\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 6\\sqrt{2}\\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 6\\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 3\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"390\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If the areas of the two triangles are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/c/36c7f3f828cf12ab9cafeffad282468a95219600.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/a/e3a8ae66ded7f33f9385a37c9cadfb82720013d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/e/f6e99ebc522d7d213d54bdb3e29bc7b10420ac0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1 &gt; A_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"65\" height=\"15\" />, we are given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/6/576373751420b56b54f2954767b7a917a8303e66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1 - A_2 = 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"106\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/d/48d4a4830324c7781752dcda73596758903e9011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{A_1}{A_2} = k^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"65\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>Plugging in the second equation into the first leads to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/0/4b05b883db44842541c7186e77e556bbc089fa35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k^2 - 1)A_2 = 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"126\" height=\"19\" />.  \n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/a/e3a8ae66ded7f33f9385a37c9cadfb82720013d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> is an integer, it can only be a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> - namely <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/3/513b693024964bdb50e453ef96a15795f1446e7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, 2, 3, 6, 9, 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"103\" height=\"16\" />.  \n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/9/ca970277a234d7ea57d6fc53aa117e24634fa54a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1 = A_2 + 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"106\" height=\"15\" />, this would lead to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/e/4ce237cfec2814966cfb5dec42bf0fb245259e3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1 = 19, 20, 21, 24, 27, 36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"194\" height=\"16\" />.  \n</p><p>This would lead to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/d/f8dca2a1724049a27f5a373c50aaddb20f2ab8af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{A_1}{A_2} = 19, 10, 7, 4, 3, 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"162\" height=\"40\" />, and the only square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.  \n</p><p>Thus, the ratio of the areas is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and hence the ratio of the sides is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/5/625885b53be76678065cd8de7fa159e040ebe848.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{4} = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" />.  The corresponding side has a length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/b/d6b0375ea5d39656d7f86f115ebfbed8c55fccb7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\cdot 2 = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"66\" height=\"14\" />, which is option <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/8/25809e4f87f20a2ee949878bc603b9eda09422ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{D}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"26\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME\" title=\"1967 AHSME\">1967 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1967 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1967 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1967\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1967 AHSME Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"1967 AHSME Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1967 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1967 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1967 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1967 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1967 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1967 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1967 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1967 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1967 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1967 AHSME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1967 AHSME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1967 AHSME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1967 AHSME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1967 AHSME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"1967 AHSME Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"1967 AHSME Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"1967 AHSME Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"1967 AHSME Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"1967 AHSME Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"1967 AHSME Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"1967 AHSME Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"1967 AHSME Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"1967 AHSME Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"1967 AHSME Problems/Problem 25\">25</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26\" title=\"1967 AHSME Problems/Problem 26\">26</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27\" title=\"1967 AHSME Problems/Problem 27\">27</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28\" title=\"1967 AHSME Problems/Problem 28\">28</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29\" title=\"1967 AHSME Problems/Problem 29\">29</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30\" title=\"1967 AHSME Problems/Problem 30\">30</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_31\" title=\"1967 AHSME Problems/Problem 31\">31</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_32\" title=\"1967 AHSME Problems/Problem 32\">32</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_33\" title=\"1967 AHSME Problems/Problem 33\">33</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_34\" title=\"1967 AHSME Problems/Problem 34\">34</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_35\" title=\"1967 AHSME Problems/Problem 35\">35</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_36\" title=\"1967 AHSME Problems/Problem 36\">36</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_37\" title=\"1967 AHSME Problems/Problem 37\">37</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_38\" title=\"1967 AHSME Problems/Problem 38\">38</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_39\" title=\"1967 AHSME Problems/Problem 39\">39</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_40\" title=\"1967 AHSME Problems/Problem 40\">40</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AHSME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AHSME Problems and Solutions\"> All A